 "title": "The toy caption model: high-level design",
 "page_title": "Toy Caption Model",
 "subtitle": "Shares with SDXL: a VAE latent, caption conditioning, training with an empty caption, and guidance. It is not a U-Net and has no text encoder.",
 "lede": "Read it top to bottom. Pictures with caption ids train a VAE that squeezes each picture into 128 numbers; a fully connected denoiser learns to guess the clean 128 numbers from a noisy copy and a caption id; and sampling calls that one denoiser three times per step and adds the answers up as the product of the two single captions. Every picture on the diagram is real: drawn by the experiment's code, sampled by its saved runs, or recorded from one retrained model, as each card says.",
